1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,850
Follow a travel request through Ironweb's live memory dashboard and Voyara.

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:09,608
The graph connects hot context, context cards, and durable evidence.

3
00:00:09,608 --> 00:00:12,850
Search, select, zoom, and inspect each memory.

4
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:16,615
The inspector exposes values, history, and source links.

5
00:00:16,615 --> 00:00:20,850
Replay selects an observed context while the graph stays current.

6
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:22,931
Nine actors are registered.

7
00:00:22,931 --> 00:00:26,850
This planning route uses seven specialists plus the memory orchestrator.

8
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:29,430
Activity separates each actor's work.

9
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:32,850
Select an event to inspect what actually happened.

10
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:38,850
Three tiers connect bounded instructions and traveler facts, task cards, and durable evidence.

11
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:45,850
Context X-ray shows each agent's captured input, allocation, supported fields, and the claims behind them.

12
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:49,850
Cache shows measured reuse, payload bytes, and entry limits.

13
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:53,850
Provider shows recorded requests and reported model token usage.

14
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:57,850
Hardware distinguishes observed memory from unavailable GPU utilization.

15
00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:01,850
Latency points expose measured context assembly and agent work.

16
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:06,850
Inspect live databases, Qdrant vectors, receipts, and masked provider identity.

17
00:01:07,150 --> 00:01:11,850
Replay, filters, keyboard shortcuts, and responsive drawers complete the controls.

18
00:01:12,150 --> 00:01:19,850
Voyara turns these capabilities into a travel experience, from destination discovery to a personal trip planner.

19
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:30,850
We request Kerala for two travelers, from December first to third, with a relaxed pace and a two hundred thousand rupee budget.

20
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:37,057
The website waits while the dashboard shows the same run.

21
00:01:37,057 --> 00:01:47,259
The orchestrator assembles context, specialists research destinations, stays, food, and experiences, then the itinerary and budget agents finish.

22
00:01:47,259 --> 00:01:52,091
These are observed events and real model calls.

23
00:01:52,091 --> 00:01:55,850
Waiting is accelerated in this edit.

24
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:57,861
Seven specialists completed.

25
00:01:57,861 --> 00:02:03,850
Voyara saves the itinerary, indicative costs, and each agent's recorded work for review.

26
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:06,733
Open the budget agent's captured context.

27
00:02:06,733 --> 00:02:12,267
Its budget is two hundred thousand rupees, backed by a specific claim and source.

28
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:14,850
Context allocation here uses UTF-eight bytes.

29
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:19,789
Now lower the budget to one hundred twenty thousand rupees.

30
00:02:19,789 --> 00:02:24,850
Saving the requirement marks the older plan stale before regeneration starts.

31
00:02:25,150 --> 00:02:29,586
Create a new outline with the same team.

32
00:02:29,586 --> 00:02:36,979
Both views remain synchronized as agents read the revised requirements and validate their results.

33
00:02:36,979 --> 00:02:45,850
The prior context stays available as history, while the new run captures the updated budget and evidence.

34
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:53,829
The budget changed from two hundred thousand to one hundred twenty thousand, with a new claim and source.

35
00:02:53,829 --> 00:02:55,850
Version two is current.

36
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:59,850
One request, visible agent work, and traceable context changes.
